dividing the numerator and denominator by $6$:\n\n$$\n\\frac{12÷6}{6÷6}=\\frac{2}{1}=2\n$$\n\nSo, $12$ dogs in $6$ houses $=2$ dogs per house."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186490252 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186073888 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "6edca753-d8cd-55a6-883b-81f80af0e0cc" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating Unit Rates as Fractions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "448249d3-e65f-58d7-aa8a-4d8b3c69d0bb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\frac{7}{2}$ dollars" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489673} {:answer/id #uuid "5907624d-87ff-5efe-be98-30c27c1c05a6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\frac{5}{2}$ dollars" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489729} {:answer/id #uuid "b56e3421-4c05-5adb-bc5a-29e7ef300c69" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\frac{4}{7}$ of one dollar" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489912} {:answer/id #uuid "ddf7aa91-b73c-5a4f-abbe-0828f0280238" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\frac{1}{2}$ of one dollar" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489997} {:answer/id #uuid "f3851c55-6bf3-50c0-bc67-1ba830e7289e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\frac{2}{7}$ of one dollar" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490038}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f3851c55-6bf3-50c0-bc67-1ba830e7289e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\frac{2}{7}$ of one dollar" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490038} :answer-field/id #uuid "32cde7f5-8b1f-53c4-a494-a727050f3e25" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490102}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "585e1f16-1ef5-574f-9665-67875bdab00b" :question/math-academy-id "q-60454" :question/problem "Sophia bought $14$ peaches for $$4.$ What is the price per peach?" :question/worked-solution "The ratio of dollars to peaches is $4:14.$ Expressing this as a fraction, we have:\n\n$$\n\\frac{4}{14}\n$$\n\nWe can reduce this fraction to its lowest terms by dividing the numerator and denominator by $2:$\n\n$$\n\\frac{4÷2}{14÷2}=\\frac{2}{7}\n$$\n\nConsequently, the price of each peach is $\\frac{2}{7}$ of one dollar."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186490273 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186073886 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "2a5b57e9-71fa-5b06-9984-c18e20f79e4e" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Missing Value in a Unit Rate"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "15f2c16c-555f-5093-80b8-9af6a8eea190" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "20" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489562} {:answer/id #uuid "19f46919-619e-5e3b-9b87-3d107a6ee44a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "17" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489571} {:answer/id #uuid "5d73d855-b72d-55b5-a89b-638743da1bdd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "14" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489738} {:answer/id #uuid "7da68662-d94c-5247-814d-3fcf2865ea86" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "15" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489799} {:answer/id #uuid "8379f504-d150-51dd-956f-0129d5c4b880" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "18" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489815}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "19f46919-619e-5e3b-9b87-3d107a6ee44a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "17" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489571} :answer-field/id #uuid "a670e60b-da88-59e1-abdf-4765a54b6df5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490168}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "87954c9a-1409-5d07-8491-76a8bb88c183" :question/math-academy-id "q-92871" :question/problem "What is the missing number in the statement below?\n\n$\\,$ $34$ books in $2$ shelves $=\\boxed{}\\,$  books per shelf." :question/worked-solution "The ratio of the number of books to shelves is $34:2.$ So we start with the ratio $34:2$ and write it as a fraction:\n\n$$\n\\frac{34}{2}\n$$\n\nWe can make a denominator of $1$ by dividing the numerator and denominator by $2$:\n\n$$\n\\frac{34÷2}{2÷2}=\\frac{17}{1}=17\n$$\n\nSo, $34$ books in $2$ shelves $=17$ books per shelf."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186490297 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186073889 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f84a62df-3608-5166-af37-4f72d8f1b821" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating Unit Rates as Decimals"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0459c439-8b14-5d9a-91df-4ca72c3317da" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$$0.09$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489525} {:answer/id #uuid "3fbd2d81-cda5-56cc-aeb4-82b360bcd345" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$$0.25$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489660} {:answer/id #uuid "43096657-4ce5-5e3c-835c-31a394a75e54" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$$0.12$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489670} {:answer/id #uuid "a3fc8369-f5cc-555f-bf36-2240c107e5c5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$$0.20$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489879} {:answer/id #uuid "cbd33eda-7c94-51b4-81af-8d5198b21dc2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$$0.15$" :db/id #edb/ref 1759218